  way to keep doing it I knew I had to  find a way to keep doing it even if I  never made money and so I did I kept  doing speaking gigs I did my website I  did my youtube channel and slowly slowly  slowly slowly it started to come in as I  figure it out  the second key important piece which is  figuring out how to bring value to other  people when you find something that you  love doing and you combine it with how  it brings value to other people that's  when you start making money it was  something that you just love doing but  nobody else likes it there's zero value  to anybody else you have a hobby you  have a hobby if you're only chasing  stuff that people like in need but you  don't like doing it you're never gonna  get great at it you might make a little  bit of money but you're never gonna get  great at it you're never gonna be  all-time  you're never gonna build a huge business  and so it's that combination of doing  work that you love doing and mix it with  where does an opportunity that people  need it's a problem that you are solving  it makes those things together you have  a super successful business rule number  eight start small entrepreneurs don't  have to be giant risk takers some  entrepreneurs have to go all-in it's the  only way they can operate earn the boats  have no plan B have no escape no  parachute all in one way trip it's the  only way they operate but there's tons  of successful entrepreneurs who win by  building sustained momentum by taking  small successful risks over  and over again but never put it all on  the line I love small starts i love  finally ways to get started on tons of  different ideas and seeing what sticks  and where my heart lies and following  those through but i'll never put in tons  of money before putting in the effort  and energy to see if i'd love it  to try to get results so I look at  YouTube as an example it's ten years of  having this channel it's wow that's  crazy  I started it just as an experiment I had  a successful website I had eight people  on my team building up this new web  business that I was a part of and I just  wanted to try YouTube I wanted to make  visual content I love learning from  successful people and so I wanted to  tell those stories in the visual way  that plus people kept asking me  questions I'd sold my company and so  they asked me questions Evan how do I do  this how do I do that great so I would  make videos answering questions for  people but I did it all myself right  like I got some friends to volunteer to  help me make some of my early videos and  then everything was me I had money I  sold my business I had a team working on  my website but I was doing this little  skunkworks project all by myself just to  go just make it happen just to see just  to see if I'd like it see if I can build  some momentum and so I researched and I  edited and I filmed I did everything and  as it started then to make some money  then I could invest that money back into  my business and then it slowly built up  to the point where we're at right now  rule number nine be the chief goal  officer you need to be people's chief  goal officer if you want to move them  into action if you want them to win you  have to speak to them in their language  and the things that they care about the  worst advice you could give somebody is  what you would do if you treat everybody  who works with you and for you like the  way you would be treated you're gonna  lose forever you're never gonna build  the organization you want because people  have different goals and it's your job  to understand what they are so I'm doing  this tour right now 90 days 23 cities I  often get asked by people  hey Evan what book should I read what  video do you recommend from your channel  for an entrepreneur time six thousand  videos the worst advice I could give is  to give a generic answer the worst  advice I could give is to one  I would watch like here's a video that I  loved the most for me to give a good  answer to you I need to know your  problem I need to be your chief goal  officer I need to understand what you're  struggling with I can give you the  greatest book recommendation of all time  but if it's not the thing that you care  about right now it's not going to serve  you and so before you give advice before  you try to help somebody else out be  their chief goal officer there's two  ways to do it understand or who and  understand their why their who is their  most important one word core value and  they're why is their purpose and their  purpose comes from their pain so look at  their who I'll use an example with Alex  who who runs trying to dance salsa for  me his who is belong his one word is  belong he wants to create a place where  people feel like they belong it's the  one word for him it's a one word for TBS  I know that's what he really cares about  for me belonging doesn't really matter  if I don't feel like I belong in a room  I'm not bothered by it I don't care what  other people think of me it's it's so  lowdown on my list of priorities and  values of what I personally care about  but for him it's number one he wants to  make people feel like they belong that's  his one word most important core value  that's his who so I understand a little  bit more about him I understand how to  push him the next is your why your  purpose comes from your pain for him he  struggled so much in in making friends  and feel accepted he had super sweaty  hands and when he held the girl's hand  he would slide out because he sweat so  much and it tied into him never feel  like he belong and so this is now his  purpose for life is to help other people  feel like they belong that there's a  space for them to come to and feel like  they belong his favorite movie of all  time is Hercules the Disney movie the  cartoon were in that song he says  something about a place where you belong  and when he hears that song he cries  great this is Alex right I might play  that song for myself and think that's a  good song I'm gonna play that song for  somebody else and they hate that song  screw Hercules amazing everybody's  different you need to be their chief  goal officer so if I'm talking out to  trying to motivate and push him and have  him build an amazing company that he's  proud of I'm gonna use words like belong  I'm gonna use movie references like  Hercules I'm gonna talk  Creed in the place where people can come  together and feel like they're finally  accepted because that's at the core what  he's all about that's me being his chief  goal officer and so you need to do that  for everybody on your team you need to  do that for every customer that you work  with stop treating everybody the same  way there's the classic rule of do unto  others as you would have them do unto  you and that's great and that's treating  people with compassion and care and  kindness but everybody's motivated by  different things and if you can only  treat people one way the way that you  would like to be treated  you're gonna only have success with a  very narrow band of people a very narrow  band of customers a very narrow band of  employees a very narrow band of partners  you're gonna stay in this tiny little  lane your entire life and never build a  huge company but if you can learn to be  somebody's chief goal officer if you can  learn to understand what drives that  moves them pushes in what they're who is  what they're why is why they're here  what they're trying to accomplish you  start building an eight-lane  superhighway and you can build a company  that can take over the world and rule  number 10 the last one before a very  special bonus clip is enjoy the process  I'm much more won enjoy the process of  the work that I'm doing then then  getting the end result when I've made my  youtube channel and we hit a million  subscribers  everybody's asked me what's the  celebration what are you guys gonna do  what's the plan no I didn't need to  celebrate we ended up doing a livestream  because I wanted to celebrate with you  guys because it was important for you  but for me I don't I don't care to  celebrate like let's keep going I love  this is the celebration making these  videos is the celebration not getting  the plaque not crossing the million aqua  XYZ only results matter of course  but the process enjoying the process and  doing difficult things is how I get  myself to take action not visualizing  the end result now I've got a special  bonus tip on how to stop saying someday  that I think you're gonna enjoy but  before that is over the three-point  landing questions let's go from just  watching the video to taking action here  we go question number one what is your  one word number two how will you start  to attack judgment and number three what  will you take in  action on today you're saying someday  because you're scared you're scared of  failing you're scared of losing money  and you're scared of what people will  say about you if you don't win but being  scared isn't a good enough reason if  you're consistently making decisions  from a place of fear you'll never do  anything great because all great things  in life come on the other side of fear  so I'm here on this tour right now  filming to my last stop here in  Cleveland and starting this tour was 90  days 23 cities I was afraid to do it  because my agent told me I needed to  charge for the event I had a hard time  charging entrepreneurs because it's  where I came from because I didn't have  a lot of money I wouldn't have been able  to afford the $45 ticket to come see  someone like this if that person came to  Toronto and so I was afraid combine that  with my biggest fear being letting  people down my biggest fear in the world  is that I'm gonna disappoint people that  people would show up and pay to see me  and I would let them down and they'd go  home feeling like it was a waste of  their money and so you combined those  things now it's not just one event that  I get to be afraid for it's every four  days for 90 days right 23 different  stops getting up and facing my fear  every single time and because I caught  that fear than I had to do it here's  what happens smart people we come up  with really smart ways as to why we  shouldn't do something right you will  come up with really smart ways why you  should not do something but deep down  you're really just afraid meanwhile  dummies are off winning off of your idea  people who aren't as smart people who  don't have as much intention a positive  goodwill people who don't have as big a  mission as you do people who don't want  to serve as much as you do they're off  there they're winning off of your idea  because they just started meanwhile  you're trying to figure out and Tinker  and plain but really you're just afraid  to execute  if you want more me check out my top 50  rules video the link is right there next  to me I think you'll enjoy it continue  to believe and I'll see you there if you  have to get motivated every single day  then you are in the wrong business the  people who win work the hardest because  they love what they do
 

